
@startuml ClassDiagram

title Todo App - Week 2 Class Diagram (Existing Design)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class TodoManager {
  + tasks: Object[]
  + container: HTMLElement

  + constructor(containerId: String)
  + loadTasks(): void
  + saveTasks(): void
  + addTask(description: String, type: String): Boolean
  + toggleComplete(id: Number): void
  + deleteTask(id: Number): void
  + renderPendingRows(): String
  + renderCompletedRows(): String
  + render(justAddedId: Number): void
}

interface "Storage" as BrowserStorage <<Browser API>> {
  + getItem(key: String): String
  + setItem(key: String, value: String): void
}

class "Document" as BrowserDocument <<Browser API>> {
  + getElementById(id: String): HTMLElement
  + title: String
}

class "HTMLElement" as BrowserElement <<Browser API>> {
  + innerHTML: String
  + querySelectorAll(selector: String): NodeList
}

TodoManager ..> BrowserStorage : uses localStorage
TodoManager ..> BrowserDocument : uses document
TodoManager "1" --> "0..1" BrowserElement : container

note right of TodoManager
  Tasks are plain JavaScript objects,
  not instances of a Task class.

  Each task contains:
  - id
  - desc
  - completed
  - priority
  - createdAt

  buildTaskRow() and
  summarizeWorkload() are
  standalone functions,
  not TodoManager methods.
end note

@enduml
